Labels written to `coder-2.json` — one row for `redistricting`, coded BLANK `direction-only` based on HB 1032 (2026): Smaltz's authorship and Yea vote establish that the legislature itself draws the maps (ruling out the commission-based rungs 1–3), but the bill's judicial-review provisions don't clearly match either rung 4 ("court oversight to prevent extreme partisan bias") or rung 5 ("without outside interference"), so I didn't pick between them by elimination.
